 "api_error_status": null,
 "result": "Route rules are deferred on the bundle and replayed onto the app at registration.\n\n1. **Deferral:** `Bundle.attach_route_rule` (`src/tessel/sansio/bundles.py:413`) is what `@bundle.route` ends up calling (`Scaffold.route` at `src/tessel/sansio/scaffold.py:344`). It calls `Bundle.record` (`bundles.py:224`), which appends a callback to `bundle.deferred_functions`. Nothing touches the app yet.\n2. **Registration entry:** `App.register_bundle` (`src/tessel/sansio/app.py:571`) calls `bundle.register(self, options)` (`app.py:596`).\n3. **Replay:** `Bundle.register` (`bundles.py:273`) builds a `BundleSetupState` via `Bundle.make_setup_state` (`bundles.py:246`). It then runs every deferred callback with that state (`bundles.py:334-335`). For bundles with a static folder it also adds the static route through `state.attach_route_rule` (`bundles.py:323-328`).\n4. **Applying rules:** `BundleSetupState.attach_route_rule` (`bundles.py:87`) applies `url_prefix`, `subdomain`, `url_defaults` and the dotted endpoint name (`name_prefix.name.endpoint`). It then calls `App.attach_route_rule` (`src/tessel/sansio/app.py:606`), which adds the rule to the app's URL map.\n5. **Nested bundles:** `Bundle.register` loops over `self._bundles` and recursively calls `bundle.register` with merged prefix, subdomain and name (`bundles.py:349-377`).",
